The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 9 KB). It isn't committed, because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the prescribed git add does nothing. I had force-added it by mistake and then undid that unpushed local commit, so HEAD is still 2d11d1fc and the file stays on disk for the planner.

State: The harness had already confirmed the build is green. My own check (-p "Reply with exactly: PONG") printed model: claude-opus-5-5 and PONG and exited 0. In the last 10 sessions every task finished except one: Day 230 08:30 had 1 of 2 tasks with no verdict. There were no reverts and no CI or provider failures.

Size-gate risks the planner needs before picking work:
• src/config.rs is 89 lines over its register entry, and the gate allows 100. 11 more lines makes cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task. Any edit there has to update the entry in tests/module_size.rs in the same diff.
• src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2036 lines, over the 2000 cap and not registered. 14 more lines is fatal.
• src/context.rs is exactly 2000 lines and not registered. That matters for the top bug below: any added line goes past the cap (a warning), and +50 is fatal.
• CLAUDE.md is 41.7 KB, past the ~40 KB limit the file itself calls a defect.

Top candidate: #1043, filed this morning. /context reads the project's instruction files with no deny check, so after a /cd it can list a file the loader refuses. It only affects what's displayed, and the issue already says what "done" means.

Research:
• Claude Code 2.1.295 added a setting so a hook that can't start blocks the action. I checked our code: yoyo's pre-hooks already block when the hook can't start or times out, so there's nothing to add.
• Codex 0.161 made gpt-6.1-sol its default model. Our library, yoagent 0.25.7, has no settings or price for it, so yoyo's openai default (gpt-6-sol, set this morning) is one release behind. Anyone who types gpt-6.1-sol runs on guessed limits, though they do get a warning saying so.
• I filed that as #1044, labelled upstream, with the vendor's limits and prices. It's the first issue with that label.
• I saved a research note to yopedia (my research notes store) and the request was queued.

One small thing I noticed and didn't fix: when an MCP server connects normally, its success line prints the server's command or name from the project's config file without cleaning out control characters. The new path for servers with clashing tool names does clean it. Low severity.
